{"case_id": "mathdial-040", "mathdial_qid": 5000505, "grade": 4, "question_type": "student_mistake", "question": "In a spelling contest held in her school, Drew got 20 questions correct, winning her the competition. She got six questions wrong, and her competitor Carla got 14 questions correct, and twice as many questions wrong as the number of questions Drew got wrong. If each competitor was asked a different question, how many questions were asked in the competition?\n\nThis is how I did it:\nDrew got a total of 20 correct and wrong answers.\nCarla got twice as many wrong answers as Drew, so Carla got 6 x 2 = 12 wrong answers.\nCarla got a total of 14 correct and wrong answers.\nTogether, Drew and Carla got 20 + 6 + 14 + 12 = 52 answers.\nSince each competitor was asked a different question, the total number of questions asked in the competition was 52/2 = 26.\n 26\n\nIs my answer right?", "problem": "In a spelling contest held in her school, Drew got 20 questions correct, winning her the competition. She got six questions wrong, and her competitor Carla got 14 questions correct, and twice as many questions wrong as the number of questions Drew got wrong. If each competitor was asked a different question, how many questions were asked in the competition?", "expected_answer": "52", "student_answer": "26", "student_confusion": "The student thought they needed to divide by two to get the number of questions asked because there were two people.", "accepted_equivalents": [], "verifiable": true, "no_forced_reveal": true, "solution_steps": 4}
